  "generation": {
    "text": "To determine how many children the adult can take to the movies with $35, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. Identify the cost of an adult's ticket and the cost of a child's ticket.\n   - The cost of an adult's ticket is $8.\n   - The cost of a child's ticket is $3.\n\n2. Let \\( x \\) be the number of children the adult can take to the movies. The total cost for the adult and the children is given by the equation:\n   \\[\n   8 + 3x = 35\n   \\]\n\n3. Solve the equation for \\( x \\):\n   \\[\n   3x = 35 - 8\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   3x = 27\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = \\frac{27}{3}\n   \\]\n   \\[\n   x = 9\n   \\]\n\nTherefore, the adult can take \\(\\boxed{9}\\) children to the movies.",
